data char_brand_admits_any_int: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "char_brand_admits_any_int" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a plain Int, including a non-scalar, is accepted at a position declared std.types Char (type Char = Int where unicode_scalar, brand(\"Char\")). So Char is a BRAND, not a type: DESIGN section 4b -- a brand is cosmetic until construction and acceptance enforce the distinction. This is BELOW THE FLOOR (values inhabit declared types), not a differentiator gap.",
    "HARM: every totality that rests on 'a Char is a scalar by construction' is unproven. std.coercion unicode_scalar_fold spells a List<Char> as host text with no typed refusal, so a surrogate reaching it through an Int retyped as Char cannot be refused by type. The 'Char by construction' reading of a call site cannot be checked by any reviewer or gate today.",
    "MEASURED, BOTH ROUTES (2026-10-05, the XL-2 CHAR follow-up PR, session sleek-fox-462). SEED (v1, frozen): gunbc run resolves char_text(c: 55296) -- a surrogate literal -- and char_text(c: x) for x: Int from text.chars() and for cp + 32 with no diagnostic at the Char parameter: ADMITTED, silently. v2 INFER (through v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_fold_member_instance fmi_assemble then fmi_infer_tree, the route the gunbc#13187 controls use): over a fixture declaring the REAL shape, type Char = Int where unicode_scalar, brand(\"Char\"), infer does not judge at all -- every case, including the Char-typed positive control, ends in a runtime pattern-match failure ('non-exhaustive pattern match on: C') before a verdict, so v2 establishes nothing for Char. Over the same fixture with the brand clause removed (a plain refinement), v2 REFUSES both the Int variable and the surrogate literal with application_argument_does_not_inhabit -- so the refinement judge exists and the brand spelling is what v2 cannot read.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder on the seed route (silent admission); v2 is loud but judges nothing (a crash, not a refusal). The class's rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths (DESIGN section 4b(1)), so it is silent wrongness until the seed route is retired or refuses.",
    "CEILING: structurally impossible -- Char a confined type whose ONLY constructor is the checked scalar constructor, so an unchecked Int has no route into Char. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: C4 constructor confinement admits Char only through its checked constructor on the native route (gunbc#13123, sole_constructor + admit_callers), SUFFICIENT FOR an Int variable at a Char position and a surrogate literal to refuse on the native route while a Char produced by the checked constructor is admitted. The same pattern is the parked nominal type-declaration plan gunbc#13024. No parallel remedy is declared here.",
    "STATE AT gunbc#13778: the public Int-to-text crossing is TYPED through std.unicode.scalar from_code_point (scalar_of_code_point, then the admitted singleton folded; Err carries the same cause); char_text is deleted and literal sites are text literals. unicode_scalar_fold is residue, not a second authority: its malformed carrier (a non-scalar member of a List<Char>) is a LOUD RUNTIME MITIGATION -- the interpreter, the coproduct lexeme spelling and the emitted runtime each fail naming the offending value, never wrapping, defaulting, skipping or returning partial text -- NOT a typed refusal and NOT structurally guaranteed. Every direct unicode_scalar_fold caller except the target-model codepoint-pattern path (module v2.std.compilers.target_model, decl target_value_expression_char_unicode_scalar, which folds a list_snoc_item of its codepoint: Char parameter) derives its members from a producer that admits scalars (censused in the PR). That one path remains a classified malformed-carrier residue: seed and emitted-native refuse loudly at the runtime representation boundary, but the path is not typed or structurally guaranteed. The rung is mitigation until the trigger holds. The fold guard's evidence on the seed route and on the emitted-native route is a RECORDED PROBE (exit status, stderr naming the value, empty stdout; receipts in the PR body), NOT an enrolled control: enrolling it would need an expected-child-failure standing arm, and the trigger makes that moot.",
    "DEPENDENTS (each rests on this class and is unproven until the trigger holds): std.coercion unicode_scalar_fold totality (gunbc#13378); the planned 'UTF-8 decoder yields Char' change; the retired bare_from_code_point row population (git history, gunbc#13778).",
    "RE-MEASURED BY EXECUTION AT HEAD 5cda378342f2acb96cc79e8febb05090084bf782 (v1 seed, `gunbc run` built and run in one remote dispatch). With `fn takes(c: Char) -> Int { 1 }`: an Int variable at `c` is ADMITTED, the surrogate literal 55296 is ADMITTED, a checked Char from `scalar_of_code_point` is ADMITTED (positive control), and a String at `c` is REFUSED (expected Product(Char), got Primitive(String)). The judge can refuse at that position, yet an Int inhabits Char: silent wrongness, below the ladder. The v2 native route is NOT established: the probe never reached infer (every `std.*` import refused resolve_module_not_found, including a fixture without Char), so no v2 rung is claimed. RUNG: below the ladder (minimum across paths). CEILING: structurally impossible (Char confined to its checked constructor). NEXT TRIGGER, CLIMBS AFTER ONE GROUNDING: C4 constructor confinement on the native route (gunbc#13123, sole_constructor with admitted callers), plus v2 reading the brand clause and resolving std.* on the native door; the seed cannot climb (v1 is semantics-frozen).",

    "CONTRARY RECEIPT, BY EXECUTION (2026-10-24, seat 18, session still-deer-41; probe head c131086ba6d5 on branch session/still-deer-41, deliberately unmerged; run by keen-heron-809 on the shared seed). The v2 native route (assemble, then v2.compiler.infer) over a one-module fixture declaring the REAL shape -- `type Char = Int where unicode_scalar, brand(...)` with the brand predicate declared the way std.types declares it (`WherePredicateMarker` and `fn brand`) -- and the body `fn f(c: Char) -> Int = c` ACCEPTS the branded Char, as it does the same fixture with the brand clause removed. So the earlier statement that v2 infer cannot read the brand spelling does not hold for the isolated shape on current main; it is superseded as a statement about the brand. WHAT IS NOT CONCLUDED: that Char is judged strictly (the fixture shows acceptance of the declared-type position, not refusal of an Int variable or a surrogate literal -- the confinement class stays open). The in-corpus ungrounded std.types.Char reference (infer_grounding_not_derived at std.unicode.char_class unicode_char_code_point) is NOT the brand: std.types does not resolve (first resolve root measured on main 12c380673f58: resolve_reason_unbound_symbol map_get, the Map import family owned by gunbc#14876), so Char never reaches infer as a grounded declaration. Trigger for that root: std.types resolving.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.types", decl_name: "Char", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.unicode.scalar", decl_name: "from_code_point", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.compilers.target_model", decl_name: "target_value_expression_char_unicode_scalar", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
